%% state_04_task_assignment.mmd — TaskAssignment Status
%% Evidence status: Implemented; dedicated assign/revoke commands have no routed delivery surface.
%% Updated 2026-07-27 (verified).
%% Ref: task_assignment model (assignment_status: active/completed/cancelled)
%% Completion can trigger missing ReviewSession creation as backstop, not guaranteed first creation path.

stateDiagram-v2
direction LR
    [*] --> active : Marketplace proposal approved<br/>ProcessApplicationCommand → syncAssignment

    active --> completed : Task enters DONE category<br/>→ auto-mark completed<br/>→ emit completion backstop flow
    active --> cancelled : Assignment revoked<br/>or assignee cleared through sync path

    completed --> [*]
    cancelled --> [*]

    note right of active
        assigned_at = auto-set on creation.
        estimated_hours, actual_hours tracked.
        assignment_type: member/external_contributor/volunteer.
        AssignTaskCommand also calls syncAssignment,
        but no production controller/route caller was found.
        Current PUT task edit updates tasks.assigned_to
        without creating a TaskAssignment row.
    end note

    note right of completed
        Completion keeps review mandatory,
        but session may already exist from
        completion-package submit path.
        If missing, backstop listener can:
        1. Create ReviewSession (status=pending)
        2. Seed reviewer assignments
        3. Use governance deadline helper
           (~72 hours default)
    end note
